# What EAS should not upload when it packs this project for a cloud build.
#
# Without this file the archive came to 336 MB and the upload died halfway with
# an EPIPE. The project sits in a subdirectory of the repository rather than at
# its root, so EAS does not apply the nested .gitignore and packs node_modules
# along with the source. It installs dependencies on the build server from
# package-lock.json regardless, so shipping them is both slow and pointless.
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/

# Generated by `expo prebuild`; EAS runs prebuild itself for a managed project.
android/
ios/

# Nothing the build needs.
__tests__/
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
